'''Lounge Gaming''' was a [[:Category:Poland|Polish]] ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' team.

==Timeline==
{{tabs dynamic
|name1=2015
|name2=2016
|This=2

|content2=
* January 27th - '''Lounge Gaming''' part ways with [[oskarish]] and add [[MINISE]] as a stand-in. <ref name="oskarish leaves">{{cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/loungegg/photos/a.1471621656477422/1503858266587094|title=Oskar "oskarish" Stenborowski isn't a part of our team anymore!|date=2016-01-27|author='''Lounge Gaming'''}}</ref>
* February 21st - '''Lounge Gaming''' sign [[MINISE]]. <ref name="minise in">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/17141-csgl-confirm-minise-signing|date=2016-02-21|title=CSGL confirm MINISE signing|publisher=[[HLTV]]|author=[[MIRAA]]}}</ref>
* May 15th - '''Lounge Gaming''' part ways with their roster. <ref name="last tournament under Lounge Gaming">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/LoungeGG/status/731136927236247553|date=2016-05-14|title=Jutro rozegramy nasz ostatni turniej!|trans_title=Tomorrow we will play our last tournament!|language={{Flag|pl}} Polish|author='''Lounge Gaming'''}}</ref>

|content1=
* September 15th - Popular betting site, CSGOLounge.com, create their own CS:GO division by signing the roster of [[Dobry&Gaming]]. <ref name="csgl sign dobrygaming">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/15946-dobry-sign-for-csgolounge|title=Dobry sign for CSGOLounge|date=2015-09-15|publisher=[[HLTV]]|author=[[MIRAA]]}}</ref>
* November 25th - '''Lounge Gaming''' sign [[mouz (Polish player)|mouz]] and move [[Loord]] to coach. <ref name="CSGL pick up mouz; Loord steps down">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/16485-csgl-pick-up-mouz-loord-steps-down|title=CSGL pick up mouz; Loord steps down|date=2015-11-25|publisher=[[HLTV]]|author=[[MIRAA]]}}</ref>
}}

